  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law, in relation to powers and duties of fire district commissioners",
    "basePrintNo": "S7014",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7014-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 37,
       "fullName": "George Latimer",
       "imgName": "434_george_latimer.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 434,
       "sessionMemberId": 717,
       "sessionYear": 2015,
       "shortName": "LATIMER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §176, Town L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7014\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the town law, in relation to powers\nand duties of fire district commissioners\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo allow all members of a fire department to be eligible to be\nnominated for the offices of chief or assistant chief.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill amends the Town Law to allow members of fire departments\nthat hold their meetings in December to be eligible for nomination for\nthe offices of chief or assistant chief regardless of whether or not\nthey are residents of New York State.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nFire departments that cover areas around the borders of New York State\nsometimes have members that are not residents of New York State. Town\nLaw already permits non-residents to be eligible for nomination to the\noffices of chief or assistant chief in fire departments that hold\ntheir annual meeting in April. This bill simply does the same for fire\ndepartments that hold their annual meeting in December.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
